#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0016 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: dataset LB without the LBSTRESC column, one row with LBDRVFL=Y. The machine-derived guard (shipped: `var_exists(\"--STRESC\") and empty(--STRESC)`) makes ABSENT != EMPTY for the Permissible-in-context column (EC-43/Fix #126) -> executes, reports nothing. Pins the fold; noViolation WITH execution."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col LBSEQ    type=Num
col LBTESTCD type=Char
col LBDRVFL  type=Char
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | GLUC | Y
